1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,636
Past the absorption edge, a photoelectron walks
into the dark.

2
00:00:04,636 --> 00:00:11,360
It does not travel alone. Neighboring atoms
scatter the wave back like whispers in an alley.

3
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:17,844
Those whispers interfere with the outgoing wave,
making oscillations above the edge.

4
00:00:17,844 --> 00:00:23,416
The rhythm depends on distance. The strength
depends on how many neighbors are out there.

5
00:00:23,416 --> 00:00:28,940
Fourier transform the oscillations, and the
local structure starts to appear from the fog.

6
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:33,960
EXAFS is not magic. It is atomic echo location
with a trench coat.
